Legal Setup
The fundamental instrument for safeguarding official statistics and minimizing the disadvantages is the legislative framework that sets out the statistical system and governs its operations. The collection of official statistics is always legally regulated by strong legislation as a prerequisite for an effective system.
The NSS is underpinned by an appropriate legislation to enable institutional and regulatory framework for its operations. The general policy of government with regard to statistical activities, that is, collection, compilation, dissemination and interpretation of statistical information for all statistics producing agencies has been embodied in the Statistics Act of 2007. The Act defines the statistical system and the roles and responsibilities of the various players within the system.
